Attitude:
- A heightened sensitivity to the religious dimension of human life, society and culture;
- An analytical capability of the plurality and complexity of religious phenomena related to Islam;
- A critical yet sympathetic understanding and appreciation of Islam.

Upon successful completion of this course, students should be able to:
1. Demonstrate a knowledge of the relationship between religion and literature;
2. Appreciate the literary value of the major works of Chinese religious classics;
3. Analyze and comment on the religious dimensions in Chinese literature.

